---
import CaseStudyBase from "../../layouts/CaseStudyBase.astro";
const L = "/case-studies/linkedin";
---

<CaseStudyBase
  title="User-centric Filtering — Case Study | Myles Lane"
  description="Reimagining LinkedIn’s connection filtering with tagging, customizable categories, and bulk messaging. A UX/UI redesign case study."
  label="LinkedIn case study"
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="cs-wrap" style="padding:72px 40px 0;">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-accent);margin-bottom:24px;">
      <span style="width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:2px;background:#0A66C2;display:inline-block;"></span>Case Study — Web / UX Concept
    </div>
    <h1 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(44px,6vw,78px);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.03em;margin:0 0 22px;max-width:14ch;">User-centric filtering</h1>
    <p style="font-size:20px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--color-navy-strong);max-width:60ch;margin:0 0 40px;">Reimagining LinkedIn’s connection filtering with tagging, customizable categories, and better space management — so professionals can manage their network without leaving the platform.</p>

    <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:48px;padding:26px 0 40px;border-top:1px solid rgb(23 36 63 / .16);">
      <div><div class="cs-meta-k">Timeline</div><div class="cs-meta-v">1 month</div></div>
      <div><div class="cs-meta-k">Role</div><div class="cs-meta-v">UX &amp; UI Designer</div></div>
      <div><div class="cs-meta-k">Tools</div><div class="cs-meta-v">Figma</div></div>
      <div><div class="cs-meta-k">Focus</div><div class="cs-meta-v">Filter · Tag · Customize</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OVERVIEW -->
  <section class="cs-wrap cs-divide" style="padding:48px 40px 80px;">
    <div class="cs-grid-overview">
      <div>
        <div class="cs-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:10px;">(01) — Overview</div>
        <div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:600;font-size:24px;letter-spacing:-.02em;">The opportunity</div>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:20px;line-height:1.62;color:var(--color-navy);margin:0;max-width:62ch;">LinkedIn is the go-to platform for networking with professionals and businesses — yet I’d spent significant time manually copying information from connection pages into a Notion dashboard, because LinkedIn lacked the features to manage a network in place. By introducing a personalized category and tagging system with real customizability, LinkedIn could improve the experience, keep professionals on the platform longer, and make networking far more efficient.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROBLEMS -->
  <section class="cs-wrap cs-divide" style="padding:48px 40px 80px;">
    <div class="cs-eyebrow">(02) — The problems</div>
    <h2 class="cs-h2" style="margin:0 0 40px;">Three things slowing people down</h2>
    <div class="cs-grid-3">
      <div class="cs-info-card" style="padding:28px;">
        <div class="cs-insight-n" style="font-size:34px;margin-bottom:16px;">01</div>
        <div style="font-weight:700;font-size:19px;margin-bottom:10px;">Limited message functionality</div>
        <p class="cs-info-p" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.58;">Searching for specific contacts or applying bulk actions is cumbersome. A search bar, checkboxes, and mass-selection tools would make managing contacts much easier.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-info-card" style="padding:28px;">
        <div class="cs-insight-n" style="font-size:34px;margin-bottom:16px;">02</div>
        <div style="font-weight:700;font-size:19px;margin-bottom:10px;">Disorganized contact management</div>
        <p class="cs-info-p" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.58;">Without personalized categories and collapsible sections, users struggle to group and retrieve important connections. A more structured system improves accessibility and workflow.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-info-card" style="padding:28px;">
        <div class="cs-insight-n" style="font-size:34px;margin-bottom:16px;">03</div>
        <div style="font-weight:700;font-size:19px;margin-bottom:10px;">Little customization</div>
        <p class="cs-info-p" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.58;">A rigid category system makes it hard to tailor filtering to specific needs. Flexible category creation lets users streamline their workflow and adapt the system to their own preferences.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SOLUTIONS INTRO -->
  <section class="cs-wrap cs-divide" style="padding:48px 40px 24px;">
    <div class="cs-eyebrow">(03) — The solutions</div>
    <h2 class="cs-h2" style="margin:0 0 8px;max-width:20ch;">A filter system that adapts to the user</h2>
  </section>

  <!-- SOLUTION 1 -->
  <section class="cs-wrap" style="padding:40px 40px 0;">
    <div class="cs-sol-head" style="margin-bottom:28px;">
      <div>
        <div class="cs-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;">Solution 01</div>
        <h3 class="cs-h3" style="font-size:30px;margin:0;">Filter rehaul</h3>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--color-navy-strong);margin:0;">I completely redesigned the Connections filter bar with collapsible categories to keep the workspace tidy, plus a search bar for quick access to filters and tags. The “Add New Filter” flow lets users create custom filters with specific tags that can be removed on hover — more control, and connection management that finally feels seamless.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="border-radius:18px;padding:clamp(18px,3vw,40px);background:#D9663B;">
      <div class="cs-browser">
        <div class="cs-browser-bar">
          <span class="cs-dot" style="background:#D9663B;"></span>
          <span class="cs-dot" style="background:#E7C24B;"></span>
          <span class="cs-dot" style="background:#5BA86A;"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-browser-video">
          <video src={`${L}/filter.mp4`} autoplay loop muted playsinline></video>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SOLUTION 2 -->
  <section class="cs-wrap" style="padding:64px 40px 0;">
    <div class="cs-sol-head" style="margin-bottom:28px;">
      <div>
        <div class="cs-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;">Solution 02</div>
        <h3 class="cs-h3" style="font-size:30px;margin:0;">Profile tags</h3>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--color-navy-strong);margin:0;">A new tagging system that integrates directly with the filter sidebar. Clicking “Tags” on a profile card opens a modal of all associated tags, with a search bar to quickly find, add, or remove them — effortless customization that helps you filter and manage connections more efficiently.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="border-radius:18px;padding:clamp(18px,3vw,40px);background:radial-gradient(120% 100% at 50% -10%,#22345B,#17243F);">
      <div class="cs-browser">
        <div class="cs-browser-bar">
          <span class="cs-dot" style="background:#D9663B;"></span>
          <span class="cs-dot" style="background:#E7C24B;"></span>
          <span class="cs-dot" style="background:#5BA86A;"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-browser-video">
          <video src={`${L}/profile.mp4`} autoplay loop muted playsinline></video>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SOLUTION 3 -->
  <section class="cs-wrap" style="padding:64px 40px 80px;">
    <div class="cs-sol-head" style="margin-bottom:28px;">
      <div>
        <div class="cs-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;">Solution 03</div>
        <h3 class="cs-h3" style="font-size:30px;margin:0;">Messaging modal</h3>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--color-navy-strong);margin:0;">A new message modal appears when users select checkboxes on profile cards — with a search bar and name tags up top for selected recipients and an optional group-name field. A toggle switches between “Group Chat” (default) and “Bulk Message,” the latter hiding the group field to streamline sending individual messages.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="border-radius:18px;padding:clamp(18px,3vw,40px);background:#D9663B;">
      <div class="cs-browser">
        <div class="cs-browser-bar">
          <span class="cs-dot" style="background:#D9663B;"></span>
          <span class="cs-dot" style="background:#E7C24B;"></span>
          <span class="cs-dot" style="background:#5BA86A;"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-browser-video">
          <video src={`${L}/messaging.mp4`} autoplay loop muted playsinline></video>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- RESEARCH -->
  <section class="cs-wrap cs-divide" style="padding:48px 40px 80px;">
    <div class="cs-eyebrow">(04) — Research</div>
    <h2 class="cs-h2" style="margin:0 0 32px;">Lots of bumps in the road</h2>
    <div class="cs-problem-2">
      <p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.62;color:var(--color-navy);margin:0;">Initial research hit hurdles — limited secondary data, and no direct LinkedIn competitor to study (a Xing account was quickly banned). So the project pivoted to user interviews with five diverse LinkedIn users. That user-centered approach delivered the real insight, and narrowed the scope from an A/B test of two concepts down to a focused redesign of the existing page.</p>
      <div style="background:var(--color-navy);color:var(--color-cream);border-radius:18px;padding:36px;">
        <div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:800;font-size:64px;line-height:1;color:#E78457;">5</div>
        <div style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;margin-top:12px;color:rgb(242 238 223 / .82);">user interviews reframed the entire project — from A/B test to focused redesign.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ITERATIONS -->
  <section class="cs-wrap cs-divide" style="padding:48px 40px 80px;">
    <div class="cs-eyebrow">(05) — Iterations</div>
    <h2 class="cs-h2" style="margin:0 0 24px;max-width:18ch;">Designing for clarity over flash</h2>
    <p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.62;color:var(--color-navy-strong);margin:0 0 36px;max-width:64ch;">At first I wanted something grand, fresh, and exciting — yet still true to the design system. I introduced a new component that looked the part but felt distinct. Testing revealed users struggled to connect it with other elements, making navigation harder. So I scaled back, aligned more closely with the existing design language, and the results were far better. Style means nothing if it isn’t intuitive and accessible.</p>
    <div style="border-radius:18px;padding:clamp(20px,3vw,40px);background:#ECE7D6;border:1px solid rgb(23 36 63 / .1);">
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid rgb(23 36 63 / .1);overflow:hidden;padding:clamp(16px,2.5vw,30px);">
        <img src={`${L}/iterations.avif`} alt="Connection-card iterations — a bold distinct tag component versus a refined Tags button" style="width:100%;display:block;" />
      </div>
      <div class="cs-grid-2" style="gap:24px;margin-top:24px;align-items:start;">
        <div style="display:flex;gap:13px;align-items:flex-start;">
          <span style="flex:none;width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;background:rgb(217 102 59 / .14);color:var(--color-accent);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:14px;margin-top:2px;">×</span>
          <div>
            <div style="font-weight:700;font-size:16px;margin-bottom:5px;">First attempt — flashy</div>
            <p class="cs-info-p" style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--color-navy-strong);">The bold tag bar looked distinct and exciting, but testing showed users couldn’t connect it to the rest of the interface — navigation got harder.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:13px;align-items:flex-start;">
          <span style="flex:none;width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;background:rgb(91 168 106 / .16);color:#3F8A55;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:14px;margin-top:2px;">✓</span>
          <div>
            <div style="font-weight:700;font-size:16px;margin-bottom:5px;">Refined — clear</div>
            <p class="cs-info-p" style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--color-navy-strong);">A simple “Tags” button that mirrors LinkedIn’s existing design language. Familiar, intuitive, and instantly understood.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROTOTYPE -->
  <section class="cs-wrap cs-divide" style="padding:48px 40px 80px;">
    <div class="cs-eyebrow">Try it</div>
    <h2 class="cs-h2" style="margin:0 0 28px;">Play with the prototype</h2>
    <div style="border-radius:20px;padding:clamp(16px,3vw,36px);background:radial-gradient(120% 100% at 50% -10%,#22345B,#17243F);">
      <div class="cs-browser" style="border-color:rgb(255 255 255 / .08);box-shadow:0 30px 70px rgba(0,0,0,.34);">
        <div class="cs-browser-bar" style="height:40px;padding:0 16px;background:#F0ECDE;">
          <span class="cs-dot" style="width:11px;height:11px;background:#D9663B;"></span>
          <span class="cs-dot" style="width:11px;height:11px;background:#E7C24B;"></span>
          <span class="cs-dot" style="width:11px;height:11px;background:#5BA86A;"></span>
          <div style="margin-left:14px;flex:1;max-width:340px;height:22px;border-radius:6px;background:#fff;border:1px solid rgb(23 36 63 / .12);display:flex;align-items:center;padding:0 12px;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--color-navy-subtle);">linkedin.com/mynetwork</div>
        </div>
        <div class="proto-viewport">
          <iframe class="proto-iframe" src="/filter-prototype/index.html" title="Interactive LinkedIn filtering prototype" allow="fullscreen"></iframe>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;margin-top:16px;">
        <a href="/filter-prototype/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.04em;color:rgb(242 238 223 / .82);border-bottom:1px solid rgb(242 238 223 / .3);padding-bottom:2px;">Open full size ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TAKEAWAYS -->
  <section class="cs-wrap cs-divide" style="padding:48px 40px 88px;">
    <div class="cs-eyebrow">(06) — Take-aways</div>
    <h2 class="cs-h2" style="margin:0 0 40px;">What I’m taking forward</h2>
    <div class="cs-grid-3" style="gap:36px;">
      <div>
        <div style="height:3px;width:40px;background:var(--color-accent);margin-bottom:18px;"></div>
        <div style="font-weight:700;font-size:19px;margin-bottom:10px;">Simplicity leads to better design</div>
        <p class="cs-info-p" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.58;">I aimed for grand solutions, but through iteration I learned that small tweaks to familiar elements are often more effective — and create a smoother, more intuitive experience.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="height:3px;width:40px;background:var(--color-accent);margin-bottom:18px;"></div>
        <div style="font-weight:700;font-size:19px;margin-bottom:10px;">Prioritize usability over flash</div>
        <p class="cs-info-p" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.58;">Flashy interactions can be tempting, but clear, intuitive designs are what let users navigate and engage with a redesign effortlessly.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="height:3px;width:40px;background:var(--color-accent);margin-bottom:18px;"></div>
        <div style="font-weight:700;font-size:19px;margin-bottom:10px;">Scale to user needs</div>
        <p class="cs-info-p" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.58;">I planned a large A/B test, then research showed it was too ambitious. Defining scope from real user data — not assumptions — kept the work focused and effective.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</CaseStudyBase>

<style>
  /* Scale-to-fit embed: render the desktop prototype at its true width (1280px)
     and scale it down to fill the panel, so the full layout is visible
     proportionally instead of squished. Aspect ratio is constant, so the box
     and the scaled iframe always match exactly. */
  .proto-viewport {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 1280 / 860;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #edeae0;
  }
  .proto-iframe {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 1280px;
    height: 860px;
    border: 0;
    display: block;
    transform-origin: 0 0;
    transform: scale(var(--proto-s, 1));
  }
</style>

<script>
  const PROTO_W = 1280;
  const fit = (vp: HTMLElement) =>
    vp.style.setProperty("--proto-s", String(vp.clientWidth / PROTO_W));
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".proto-viewport").forEach((vp) => {
    fit(vp);
    new ResizeObserver(() => fit(vp)).observe(vp);
  });
</script>
